    "millsfield:images_texts": [
      "For Your Safety\nBOEING 737-200\n-\nalsha\nAIRLINES®\nFor your safety, obey \"Fasten Seatbelt\" and\n\"No Smoking\" signs. Follow all instructions given\nby crewmembers. For the safety of others, please\ndo not remove card from aircraft.\nPassengers should open exits in an emergency\nonly if a Flight Attendant cannot reach the exit.",
      "A\nEXIT\nA2\n(EXIT\nB1\nB2\nEXIT\n*14\nThe Federal Aviation Administration (FAA) requires\nthat passengers in exit rows be able to speak and read\nEnglish. They must also be able to understand the\npassenger safety information card and oral commands\nfrom the crew. Other requirements are listed on this\ncard. If you are in an exit row and cannot meet all\nthese requirements, or do not wish to perform the exit\nrow functions, ask the Flight Attendant to move you.\nYou need not explain why. Just say \"l do not want to\nsit in an exit row.\"\nA3\nA4\nA5\nLa Administraci?n (FAA) Federal de la Aviaci?n\nrequiere que pasajeros en filas de salida son\ncapaces de hablar y leer ingl?s. Ellos deben ser\ntambi?n capaces de entender la tarjeta de\ninformaci?n de seguridad de pasajero y ?rdenes\norales de la tripulaci?n. Otros requisitos se listan en\nesta tarjeta. Si usted est? en una fila de la salida y\nno puede encontrar todo estos requisitos, ni no\ndesear realizar las funciones de la fila de la salida,\npregunte al Asistente del Vuelo para moverlo. Usted\nnecesita no explica por qu?. Diga apenas \"yo no\nquiero sentarse en un fila.\" de la salida\nB3\nB4\nB5\nCode 1959",
      "SEC\nSEC\n2\n3\nSEC\nSEC\n1 If yellow streamer is present,\n2\npull to start the flow of oxygen.\nOR\nCopyright © Interaction Research Corporation, 2006, Olympia, WA, USA\nAll Rights Reserved. Code 1959 www.safetycards.com\n360-357-4454\nFinal assembly of this airplane was completed in the United States. Rev. 06-06\n2011126"
    ],
